WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.800
Привет, Фрэнс!

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:03.560
Welcome to привет, русский эпизод 37.

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:07.120
Это 10 июня 2026 года.

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:07.940
I am all ya.

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:10.360
Today's lesson is going to be a fun one.

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:11.180
Поехали.

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:13.740
Today our word is Koshka.

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:14.540
Koshka.

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:17.280
The pronunciation breaks into two clear parts.

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:18.540
Kosh and K.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:23.080
Imagine a cozy cat, CoreLab on a windowsill saying Kosh-kosh.

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:24.600
This word means cat.

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:25.960
Repeat after me.

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:26.580
Koshka.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:27.240
Koshka.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:30.260
Now that you know Kosh-k, let's learn sabaka.

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:31.440
Sabaka.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:32.520
It means dog.

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:33.780
Repeat after me.

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:34.960
Sabaka.

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:36.440
Sabaka.

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:37.960
У меня есть sabaka.

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:39.520
That means I have a dog.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.280
The memory hook remains you.

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:42.880
That the word sounds like so back.

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:45.580
As if your dog comes running back to you.

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:47.600
Say the full sentence slowly now.

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:49.740
У меня есть sabaka.

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:52.160
Then try it once more at normal speed.

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:54.060
Next comes Ptitsa.

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:54.960
Ptitsa.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:55.840
It means bird.

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:56.920
Repeat after me.

00:00:57.060 --> 00:00:57.660
Ptitsa.

00:00:58.060 --> 00:00:58.660
Ptitsa.

00:00:58.740 --> 00:00:59.780
Ptitsa летает.

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:01.320
That means the bird fly.

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:05.740
Think of the sound Ptitsa like a tiny twit from a bird high in the sky.

00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:08.880
Practice the sentence by saying Pti.

00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:09.860
Sabaka.

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:11.020
Yet after me.

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:13.160
Now repeat the whole phrase again.

00:01:13.660 --> 00:01:14.100
Now try.

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:14.720
Рыба.

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:15.680
Рыба.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:16.680
It means fish.

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:17.980
Repeat after me.

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:18.520
Рыба.

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:20.380
Рыба плавает.

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:21.980
That means the fish swims.

00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:25.560
The hook works because Рыба rhymes with SIBA.

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:29.060
Helping you picture yourself seeing the fish in clear water.

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:30.920
Say Рыба плавает.

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:31.560
Slowly.

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:33.400
Then again at regular pace.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:35.040
Let's add Медведь.

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:36.200
Медвыет.

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:37.100
It means bear.

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:38.240
Repeat after me.

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:39.020
Медвыет.

00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:40.040
Медвыет.

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:41.860
Медведь большой.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:43.680
That means the bear is big.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:49.140
The sound Медвыет brings to mind a wise medicine bear that knows many things.

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:50.800
Say Медвыет.

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:51.500
Большой.

00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:52.480
Афтер Митвайс.

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:54.080
Киры заяц.

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:55.080
Заяц.

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:56.540
It means hair or rabbit.

00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:57.600
Repeat after me.

00:01:57.920 --> 00:01:58.400
Заяц.

00:01:58.980 --> 00:01:59.580
Заяц.

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:00.980
Заяц прыгает.

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:02.580
That means the hair jumps.

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:07.700
The hook заяц helps because it feels like the animal hopping fast across a field.

00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:12.180
Practice заяц прайгает right now for slowly and then naturally.

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:14.080
Now we have лошад.

00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:14.800
Лошад.

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:15.660
It means horse.

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:16.960
Repeat after me.

00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:17.620
Лошад.

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:18.560
Лошад.

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:19.660
Лошад бежит.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:21.440
That means the horse runs.

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:25.460
Picture a low shadow galloping when you hear low shot.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:28.300
Say low shot бежит after me.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:28.780
Boss.

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:29.940
Then once more.

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:30.900
At normal speed.

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:32.120
Meet Sloan.

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:32.860
Sloan.

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:33.940
It means elephant.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:35.500
Repeat after me.

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:36.200
Sloan.

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:37.140
Sloan.

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:37.740
Sloan.

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:38.440
Большой.

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:40.220
That means the elephant is big.

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:42.860
The word Sloan feels slow and long.

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:45.540
Just like an elephant's trunk, stretching forward.

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:46.980
Repeat Sloan.

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:47.580
Большой.

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:48.140
Clearly.

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:50.100
Our last word is мыш.

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:50.740
Мыш.

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:51.660
It means mouse.

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:52.960
Repeat after me.

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:53.500
Мыш.

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:54.080
Мыш.

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:54.840
Мыш.

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:55.440
Маленькая.

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:57.100
That means the mouse is small.

00:02:57.620 --> 00:02:57.900
The hook.

00:02:58.200 --> 00:02:59.560
Мыш works like Mish.

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:03.080
Bring in up the idea of a tiny mischievous mouse darting about.

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:03.960
Say.

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:04.520
Мыш.

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:05.180
Маленькая.

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:05.840
After me.

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:06.300
Boss.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:08.140
Russian nouns have gender.

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:12.900
Most animal names ending in art, feminine, like koska and sabaka.

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:15.720
We use maya for may with feminine words.

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:17.720
Майя koska means my cat.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:19.600
Майя sabaka means my dog.

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:23.360
Compared to English, where may stays the same for everything.

00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:27.120
Мой медведь means my bear, because bear is masculine.

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:30.700
In Russia, many families keep cats as beloved pets.

00:03:31.240 --> 00:03:34.740
You will often see stray cats cared for in quarters and parks.

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:36.880
Russians have a special saying.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:38.740
Без кошки дом не дом.

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:41.840
It means a house without a cat is not a home.

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:46.060
The phrase shows how Russians value these furry friends in daily life.

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:46.660
Say.

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:49.460
Без кошки дом не дом, slowly with me.

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:51.440
Do you remember what кошка mean?

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:55.700
Draw your favorite animal and say its Russian name out loud three times,

00:03:56.060 --> 00:03:57.120
while pointing to it.

00:03:57.800 --> 00:04:01.500
Walk around your home and name every animal you see using today's words.

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:04.840
Try making a simple sentence like это кошка.

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:06.600
That means this is a cat.

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:10.600
For adults, the same walk works well in your neighborhood too.

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:12.740
Want to know a secret about кошка?

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:16.900
Did you know that the Russian word кошка and the English word cat

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:19.680
are actually cousins from the same ancient route?

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:24.000
They both come from a very old sound people made to call cats,

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:27.720
something like cut or cadoo thousands of years ago.

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:32.000
This word travelled through Latin cathos into many European languages.

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:36.080
While in Russian, it became кошка, keeping that soft care sound.

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:40.360
Be careful though, the Russian word mush sounds a bit like mouse

00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:42.320
and means exactly the same thing.

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:46.060
Yet mush can also trick you because it ends with a soft sign

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:47.420
that changes the pronunciation.

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:49.880
Next time you see the English word cat,

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:52.160
remember it is cousins with кошка.

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:54.880
They both come from that ancient calling sound.

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:58.280
That connection is your secret shortcut to remembering it forever.

00:04:58.600 --> 00:04:59.700
You did great today.

00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:03.140
Say today's words out loud one more time and there yours.

